course: dictionary
lesson: 9871
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word table is a good example. Its most common meaning is a piece of furniture with a flat top on legs: «Then she put it on the kitchen table and went to bed.»
explain: Table can also mean a list of numbers or words in rows and columns, like a times table or a timetable. Look at the words around it to see which meaning fits. A sentence about numbers or rows is a clue that you need the list meaning.
explain: Table can even mean the people sitting at it. «In front of the whole table» means in front of everyone sitting there, not in front of a piece of furniture. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Table is a noun: one table, two tables.
fact: A table can be a piece of furniture with a flat top on legs.
fact: A times table is a list of products, such as 3 × 1, 3 × 2 and 3 × 3.
fact: «At the table» means sitting in your place to eat, and waiting until everyone is seated and served before you start.
fact: «Set the table» and «clear the table» are phrases about getting ready for a meal and taking things away afterwards.
exercise: «Then she put it on the kitchen table and went to bed.» What is a table here? | A group of people eating together | A list of numbers in rows and columns | A kind of game | *A piece of furniture with a flat top on legs
exercise: What is a times table? | A set of pictures of animals | *A list of products, such as 3 × 1, 3 × 2 and 3 × 3 | A piece of furniture for eating | A rule for drawing circles
exercise: «...in front of the whole table, and the new boy leaves red-faced.» What does table mean in this sentence? | The kitchen floor | A flat top on legs | A list of words in rows | *The people sitting at the table
test: «Set the table» means getting ready for a meal. What does table mean in this phrase? | *A piece of furniture | A kind of cloth | A list of numbers | A row of chairs in a hall
test: Which phrase uses table to mean a set of numbers in rows and columns? | Kitchen table | *Times table | Clear the table | Lay the table
exam: «At the table you wait until everyone is seated and served.» Which meaning of table fits this? | *The place where people sit together to eat | A sheet of paper with a grid | A piece of wood to cut on | A list of numbers in rows and columns
